{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"87ba46c1c0ac06d6bd8fd7aa0871116ada4c961d9f2489170fe6c21b5c1d3647","digest":{"component_or_area":"config schema and deprecation framework","key_entities":["src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/_deprecations.py","ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses","JiraConfig.resolved_statuses","adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py","docs/config.md","docs/user-guide.md","scripts/check_config_reads.py","classify_probe_response","f020","f408-64ad-ee41-46b6"],"problem_keywords":["deprecation","orphaned config keys","resolved_statuses","inert after refactor","user-facing retirement"],"propositions":["The resolved_statuses config keys (jira and reconciler) became inert after task f020 deleted the inbound absence-probe port and its only reader, classify_probe_response.","The keys were live and behaviour-affecting in shipped release v0.10.1 where the inbound probe was reachable and adapters/jira/probe.py read jira.resolved_statuses; they only became dormant in v0.11.0.","Operators were documented to set these keys to handle self-hosted workflow name differences, so existing pyproject.toml files plausibly carry them, making hard removal a genuine upgrade hazard.","The decision is to deprecate with warning (not remove now), keep parsing and validation unchanged, remove only the write-only DC plumbing, and defer hard removal to a follow-up ticket requiring operator sign-off."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787363270583527001,"uuid":"bd9ebbfb-b40b-403e-8fe6-dfda18e5a088"}